==Coptic==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|cop|ⲉϭⲱϣ||S|A}}

===Etymology===
<div>From {{inh|cop|egx-dem||{{t2i-Egyd|j-2|kš|T14-N25}}|tr={{l|egx-dem|jkš}}|Nubia, Ethiopia, Nubian, Ethiopian}}, from {{inh|cop|egy|kꜣš|<hiero>k-A-S:N25</hiero>|tr={{l|egy|kꜣš}}|Kush}}.</div>

===Noun===
{{cop-noun|m|ⲉⲑⲁⲩϣ|f=ⲉⲑⲟϣⲓ}}

# {{lb|cop|Bohairic}} {{l|en|Ethiopian}}, {{l|en|Nubian}}

===Adjective===
{{head|cop|adjective|g=m}}

# {{lb|cop|Bohairic}} {{l|en|Ethiopian}}, {{l|en|Nubian}}

====Usage notes====
ⲉⲑⲱϣ denominates "black person", living in the parts of Africa south of the Aswan, i.e. the Horn of Africa and Sudan. In the Septuagint, {{l|cop|ⲡⲕⲁϩⲓ ⲛ̀ⲧⲉ ⲛⲓⲉ̀ⲑⲁⲩϣ|t=land of the Ethiopians}} and {{l|cop|ⲛⲓⲉⲑⲁⲩϣ}} translates {{cog|hbo|כּוּשׁ}} (kûš) and {{cog|grc|Αἰθιοπία}}, the Biblical term for "black Africa". In the latter Coptic literature and toponymy ⲉⲑⲱϣ is used as an equivalent of {{cog|ar|حبش|tr=habaš|t=Abyssinian}}.

===References===
* {{R:cop:Vycichl}}
* {{R:cop:Kircher}}

{{c|cop|Ethnonyms}}

