<div>From {{inh|cop|egx-dem||{{t2i-Egyd|ḥ-2|l|P5|w-Y1}}|tr={{l|egx-dem|ḥl}}|to fly}}, from {{inh|cop|egy|ḥrj|<hiero>Hr:r-N31</hiero>|tr={{m|egy|ḥrj}}|to be(come) far, to fly off}}.</div>

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|cop|/hoːl/}}

====Verb====
{{head|cop|verb|stative|ϩⲏⲗ}}

# {{lb|cop|intransitive|Sahidic|Akhmimic|Bohairic|Fayyumic}} to [[fly]]
#* Revelation 12
#*: ⲁⲩⲱ ⲁⲩϯ ⲛⲧⲉⲥϩⲓⲙⲉ ⲛⲧⲛϩ ⲥⲛⲁⲩ ⲛⲁⲉⲓⲧⲟⲥ ϫⲉⲕⲁⲁⲥ '''ⲉⲥⲉϩⲱⲗ''' ⲉⲃⲟⲗ ⲉⲧⲉⲣⲏⲙⲟⲥ ⲉⲡⲉⲥⲙⲁ ⲉⲧⲟⲩⲛⲁⲥⲁⲛⲟⲩϣⲥ ⲛϩⲏⲧϥ ⲛⲟⲩⲟⲉⲓϣ ⲙⲛ ϩⲉⲛⲟⲩⲟⲉⲓϣ ⲙⲛ ⲧⲡⲁϣⲉ ⲛⲟⲩⲟⲉⲓϣ ⲙⲡⲙⲧⲟ ⲉⲃⲟⲗ ⲙⲡϩⲟϥ.
#*:: Two wings of the great eagle were given to the woman, that she might '''fly into''' the wilderness to her place, so that she might be nourished for a time, and times, and half a time, from the face of the serpent.
# {{lb|cop|intransitive|Bohairic|Fayyumic}} to [[go]]

=====Conjugation=====
Though the tables below show the expected conjugation with the infinitive as root, in fact for this verb the infinitive is never used with durative sentences (which must instead take the stative).
{{cop-conj|a=1|b=1|f=1|s=1}}

